WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.119 --> 00:00:06.830
(Maddie yawns)

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.640
- [Mark] All right, Maddie.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.690
Maddie, welcome back.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.640
How have things been since we
spoke about a month or so ago?

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.200
- [Maddie] Crazy.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.450
- [Mark] What's goin' on?

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.440
- Everything's changing.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.600
- [Mark] We were just
talking a little bit about

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.880
the drugs that are on the street,

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.500
seems like that's changed
in the last week or two.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.080
- Well, it's actually...

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.630
Okay, to be completely honest,

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.020
it's been like four
months, around that time,

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.770
everywhere has changed and
prices have gone up because,

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:44.750
also I think one of the more
so like main people kinda

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.740
moved to a new city.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.703
It's always like, with that being said,

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.550
instead of getting a whole ounce

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:59.680
which is like 14 gram, which
is nowhere, seven is a half.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:00.513
So yeah,

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.950
14 grams is like $230

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.130
instead of what we used
to get it at like 120.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:13.330
So people are not being
able to do their jobs.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:16.323
And then on top of that,
they're mixing fentanyl.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.650
They're not putting in the right chemicals

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.680
or cooking it right,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.480
which is causing people to go crazy.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.510
And then people who are doing
drugs such as (mumbles),

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.240
crack, crystal,

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.860
weed,

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.430
all in one,

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.920
they're really starting to go crazy

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:34.950
'cause they're mixing the drugs

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.200
and not taking care of themselves.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.673
And then listening to people
who have spiritual opinions.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.550
- [Mark] So how are
things for you personally?

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.383
- Personally,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.250
I kind of moved downtown actually,

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.753
instead of the back streets.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.130
I lost a few people who
I thought I'd trusted

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.123
because of,

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:02.490
not liking certain
things that they would do

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.933
and sticking up for myself.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.820
I had to go through some
more abuse with some friends

00:02:15.626 --> 00:02:17.760
who I really looked up to but,

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.690
I know they're going through something

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.163
and I'm not mad at them.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.560
But to a certain point

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.830
I had to just walk away
from that situation

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.033
without getting myself killed or anything.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.770
And there's been just a lot of drama

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.616
because people are getting competitive.

00:02:39.616 --> 00:02:41.858
(siren wailing)

00:02:41.858 --> 00:02:42.707
- [Mark] People are getting what?

00:02:42.707 --> 00:02:43.595
- Competitive.

00:02:43.595 --> 00:02:44.936
- [Mark] Competitive.

00:02:44.936 --> 00:02:47.440
- They're just like, if
they don't like an answer

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.130
then they get super mad.

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:49.963
Or

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.030
like, if let's say if it's over a guy

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:55.470
then the girls get super like...

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:59.030
They'll gang up on the person.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:02.880
And then with the whole
thing that happened

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.820
with the black guy who
died from the police

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.363
it's kind of made it harder
on white people out here.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:13.830
I've had a couple of
fights because I am white

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.473
and I didn't even know
the people, but yeah.

00:03:21.882 --> 00:03:24.860
- [Mark] Do you long for a life

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:28.690
outside of this Skid Row situation?

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:29.523
You do?

00:03:29.523 --> 00:03:30.356
'Cause last time we spoke,

00:03:30.356 --> 00:03:31.189
you were talking about

00:03:31.189 --> 00:03:32.080
how you're getting comfortable with it

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.930
and you kind of like it in some ways.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:38.080
- I am comfortable with
it but at the same time

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.220
it's always pushing me
to like want to do better

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.137
'cause after being out
here, you kind of like,

00:03:45.137 --> 00:03:46.607
"Oh, this is the shit.

00:03:46.607 --> 00:03:48.680
"No rules, no anything."

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.010
And that's this whole fucking lie.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.750
And it's harder on a lot of people.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.853
And then you watch people die.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:57.810
You hear about stuff.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:00.090
You watch guys beat up the girls

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.293
or boss them around.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.290
Girls out here are...

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.590
Well, everybody out here
is just manipulative.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.950
Nobody really tells the
truth unless it's for...

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.190
I should know nobody tells the truth.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.203
They just all lie.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.300
And then when somebody
does tell the truth,

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.810
they kind of get blamed for it.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.610
Like I've noticed a lot,

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:27.030
everybody blames me.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.090
I'm the first to get blamed.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:33.280
And that's because I'm the
youngest or I'm the white girl

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:37.320
or it's just the first thing they point at

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:38.963
because that's the easiest.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:42.020
I've seen that a lot

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.940
which maybe it's the crowd
of people I hang out with.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.433
And I haven't really been hanging
out with that many people.

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:54.670
But it's hard 'cause I
don't lie. I don't steal.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:58.880
And it's been proven over and
over and over again to them.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.400
But it doesn't matter 'cause

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.570
it's all about the drugs
out here really to them.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.920
It's the drugs and the sex.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:15.390
They don't think about like
what could become out of it

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:19.653
or whose feelings are hurting or anything.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.660
- [Mark] But I think a lot of
my viewers, including myself,

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:26.200
watch your story, listen
to your story and,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.150
think it's a 16-year old like yourself,

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:33.650
shouldn't be on Skid Row,
homeless, doing crystal meth.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.500
And what are you doing for money now?

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:37.723
- I'm still recycling.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:40.703
I trade stuff.

00:05:40.703 --> 00:05:43.313
So when I get shoes or
something I sell them.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.750
Or when the looting was going on,

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.730
there was a lot of...

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:49.710
I did not go looting,

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.747
but yeah there's a lot of merchandise

00:05:51.747 --> 00:05:52.580
(mumbles) money off.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:53.413
- [Mark] I'm sure.

00:05:53.413 --> 00:05:54.363
It all came down to Skid Row.

00:05:55.787 --> 00:05:56.787
- [Mark] So,

00:05:58.840 --> 00:05:59.990
what would help Maddie?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.180
What's out of your reach right
now that actually could maybe

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.640
- School.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.363
I can do school and sports.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.423
- [Mark] You would do
what? Finish high school?

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:13.400
- I'd be starting 10th grade.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.250
'Cause I finished ninth grade,
but never made it to 10th.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.430
- [Mark] So like some kind of housing?

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:20.773
Maybe away from Skid Row?

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:25.630
- I'm okay. I'll just get a SRO and a job.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:27.110
'Cause an SRO,

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.350
even though they're disgusting,

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.070
they're the way to go actually.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.730
Think about it $45 a month

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.290
and it covers water and electricity.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.559
- [Mark] No, but staying on Skid Row,

00:06:35.559 --> 00:06:37.690
I see that as problematic, no?

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:38.560
- Not if you're inside,

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:41.680
like if you're in an apartment
people can't mess with you.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:42.950
- [Mark] No, I'm not
worried about the danger.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:43.930
I mean, it helps with danger.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.210
It helps with comfort

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.083
but it's the drugs that
are still a problem.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.400
- No, not really.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.810
I've been leaning more so off the drugs

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:56.730
'cause they have been
actually really changing.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.340
- [Mark] So regardless of where,

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.940
but some kind of housing
provides stability for you?

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.000
- I really just think like

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:06.793
school.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.910
I just really want to get back in school.

00:07:10.787 --> 00:07:13.610
And then I'ma start doing some classes

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:15.593
at the college tech thing,

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.423
LATTC.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:21.423
And

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:26.820
right now, even though I
kinda moved to a new place

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.420
and everything,

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:33.060
I am living with my uncle and
the girl that I call my mom

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:33.893
even though she's not my mom.

00:07:33.893 --> 00:07:36.410
And they've been giving me more structure.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:38.060
- [Mark] Oh, so you've been
staying with your uncle?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.660
- He's not really my uncle,
but I call him my uncle.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.830
- [Mark] Who are they?
They're an older couple?

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:46.663
- Yeah.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.480
- [Mark] And they're
looking out for you or?

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.313
- Yes.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:53.030
I have like rules to stay there.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.848
Like I have to clean,

00:07:54.848 --> 00:07:56.160
(mumbles) at a certain time.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.670
I have to call them every
30 minutes when I'm gone.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:00.298
So the normal kid.

00:08:00.298 --> 00:08:02.670
- And this is what?
This is their apartment?

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:06.203
- No, it's still a tent,
but better than nothing.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:08.953
- [Mark] So you're still
in a tent on the street?

00:08:13.046 --> 00:08:14.790
- But I haven't like...

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:17.763
Learning a lot more and,

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.200
it has been more like so family-like

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:24.150
but not too overwhelming.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.340
And they're not trying to control me

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:28.150
'cause when you try to control a teen,

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:31.210
they're gonna run or
you're gonna push them away

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.233
being overbearing.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.523
And being out here,

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:39.523
I've gotten all my partying out of me.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.880
Partying sucks. It doesn't seem fun.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:46.070
Doing drugs is not as fun as it thinks,

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:48.973
'cause all you do out here
is just party drink, smoke.

00:08:50.534 --> 00:08:52.280
And it's nothing.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.113
It's not life.

00:08:53.113 --> 00:08:56.660
And most people get carried
away when they're in college

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.210
or drop out of college,

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:01.060
or when they're young adults.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.810
Kind of gets stuck in that because,

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.980
they haven't done it at a young age.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.320
- [Mark] Well, you see
plenty of people here

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.570
that are double, triple,
four times your age

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.370
and where are they?

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:12.980
Where do they?

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:15.700
- [Maddie] A lot of people
who are older than me,

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:19.053
I would say I'm a lot more
mature than most people.

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:22.960
And then when it comes
through like rule following.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:23.793
- No, but my point is

00:09:23.793 --> 00:09:25.583
they're still living
on the street in tents.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.020
- Yeah, they don't really care.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:31.870
They don't see themselves going anywhere.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.393
But I don't blame them 'cause,

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.620
a lot of them have been in jail or prison.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.430
And I mean, since they're kids like

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.920
younger than what I am right now,

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.070
and it kind of fucks them up,

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:46.040
like they've had that
structure all that time,

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:47.310
but they're not able...

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.500
The government doesn't see them as equal.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:53.760
And so like, let's say a
person get hurt by somebody,

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.520
and do something to that person,

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.883
at like the age of 10.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.883
And then be in jail until they're 21.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.120
It's really not fair for them mentally

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:09.340
'cause they're missing so many things.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:13.050
And then they don't have
an equal opportunity.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.170
So they just might as
well stay where they are.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:21.170
It's like people who have
histories shouldn't really be,

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:24.900
held accountable to it for the most part.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:26.550
I think they should get an equal,

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.790
opportunity, when they're out here,

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.310
or just out here in the world
after they serve their time

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.600
because they already served their time.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:38.500
They're already punished for
something that they've done.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:39.660
So why punish them more?

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.371
That's why they're out here.

00:10:41.371 --> 00:10:43.920
Most people out here hate it.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:46.110
Most people out here know that

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:47.430
there is nothing better for them

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:50.103
because they can't get a
job like a normal person.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:53.630
They've lost so many
time people judge them

00:10:54.527 --> 00:10:56.023
because of the tattoos that they have,

00:10:57.350 --> 00:11:00.430
or things that are on their records.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.000
And

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:02.833
it's not fair.

00:11:02.833 --> 00:11:05.630
It's just whatever.

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:09.300
Like how recently there was a cop in LAPD

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:12.510
who got taken off of the force,

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:13.690
because some girl said

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:18.140
he raped her so many years ago

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:21.140
but they had no evidence,
but they didn't question her.

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:23.490
Why would she just come
so many years later

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.008
when she could have done
it right then and there

00:11:26.008 --> 00:11:28.180
because they're not far in age.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:33.180
So, with that being said,
just from that story,

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:35.830
it's like did he even rape her?

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:37.220
Or did she get mad at him

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:41.460
and just say that so many years later

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:42.503
just to ruin his

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:45.690
life?

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:48.090
'Cause a lot of people
just want to ruin people,

00:11:49.897 --> 00:11:54.150
just to cover up somebody
else or save themselves.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:57.193
- [Mark] But what I see
in regards to you is,

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:00.250
if you spend enough time
down here in Skid Row

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:03.750
you'll eventually probably
get a similar arrest record

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:08.430
and you'll start doing more
extreme things to make ends meet

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:11.000
or to get your drug or do whatever.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:14.550
And that's what I think, at your young age

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:19.990
I think myself and a lot of
viewers see an opportunity

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:22.660
to change your direction.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:23.670
- I wouldn't like...

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:26.793
It does kind of seem
like that, but for me,

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:32.550
I thought that I would be
more like following people.

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:35.950
I'm actually starting to more
so veer towards my own lane.

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:36.783
- [Mark] That's great.

00:12:36.783 --> 00:12:37.770
- Even though it's harder

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.083
because there's a lot of hate out here.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.463
It scares me. It scares
me seeing everybody else.

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.240
- [Mark] Well, there's a much better life

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.460
outside of Skid Row in
case you're not aware.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:50.640
- Yeah. I know that.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:51.803
I know that for sure.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:54.093
And

00:12:55.014 --> 00:12:56.860
it's like following rules.

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:59.970
Okay, I used to like
being a rule breaker, but,

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:02.493
ooh, I don't even like jaywalking now.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:05.720
It's like,

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.680
or like if a police comes
just shut the fuck up

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.180
and let them do their talking.

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:12.810
'Cause I really,

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:13.643
I don't know.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:15.600
I want to become a nurse

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.917
and a lot of people have been saying,

00:13:17.917 --> 00:13:19.863
"Oh, why don't you go into nursing?

00:13:19.863 --> 00:13:22.807
"Why do you go do the
trade college because,

00:13:22.807 --> 00:13:24.507
"you like to take care of people."

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.210
But it's whatever,

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:31.607
I'm kind of stuck in a
spot right now, but...

00:13:38.679 --> 00:13:39.512
- [Mark] All right, Maddie.

00:13:39.512 --> 00:13:40.550
Well, thank you for coming back

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:42.683
and filling us in on
what's going on with you.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.384
And let's see

00:13:45.384 --> 00:13:48.034
if we can kind of maybe do
something to help you out.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.500
- I should have like a... I don't know.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.510
Like almost like a camp
for people to come out here

00:13:58.597 --> 00:14:00.940
and like spend a week or two

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:04.140
and see what like have
a different viewpoint of

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:07.620
what it's like on the streets

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:09.420
and what it could be like for people

00:14:10.854 --> 00:14:12.840
but also how people are out here

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:16.080
'cause even though they
seem like they're crazy,

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.560
a lot of them have stories,

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:21.763
and are just mentally ill
or just act like it because,

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.580
after a while people like
to tear you down out here

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:30.403
and really don't like
anybody being happy because

00:14:30.403 --> 00:14:31.823
they're not happy.

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:39.590
Or people can't stick up
for the wrongdoing because,

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.943
that person has a name or reputation.

00:14:44.585 --> 00:14:46.690
And we can't change that

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:49.410
because people are scared 'cause,

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:51.390
it is true people do get killed out here

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.480
or found behind dumpsters.

00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:55.340
And it's no joke.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.190
And a lot of people get away with it.

00:15:01.696 --> 00:15:05.113
(vehicle engine revving)

